  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\n   - Central Idea: Improve a symmetric step function by iteratively refining symmetrized versions and exploring complementary structures to reduce maximum correlation\n   - Selection Rationale: Symmetric functions reduce correlation due to centered structure. Complementary functions provide additional low-correlation configurations at similar lags\n   - Bottleneck: Original function evidenced gaps at symmetric lags (k and -k), which could be addressed by combination\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\n   - Representation: Step function with discontinuities enforced via projections\n   - Variables: Normalized steps forming probability distribution\n   - Objective: C5 = max\u2096 \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx over discrete grid\n   - Constraints: \u2211h_i = n/2, 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1 \u2200i\n   - Operations: Cross-correlation computation, symmetry enforcement via projection\n   - ProxyGradient: Available via finite difference from least-entropy surrogates\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\n   - Validation: Phase-validate symmetry by enforcing h(x) + h(2-x) = 1 normalization\n   - Symmetrize(): Project input into complementary space via orthogonal projection onto L2([0,2])\n     h_sym[i] = 1 - h[2*(n-1)-i] for valid indices\n   - Refine(lower=0, upper=1):\n     Evaluate f(x) = template(x) + \u03c3(x)*N(0,1) + shift, apply projection\n     Local min iteration with line search on projected samples\n   - Hyperparameters:\n     - \u03c3: 0.2 (initial), decreases linearly to 0.1 over iterations\n     - Iterations: 100 warmup steps, 150 local refinement\n     - RestartTol: 1e-6 score improvement or 300 seconds\n     - ProjectionSteps: 300 iterations with step size 1/t\n   - ScoreComparison: Cast geometric mean of scores and apply weighted self-similarity metric\n     score(\u03b8) = \u220f_{k=1}^m (C5(h_\u03b8) + \u03b1)^{1/2} - holds best solution\n\n4. Search Choices:\n   - BaseImplementation: Levenberg-Marquardt on projected constraints\n   - Metamethod: Followed by resilience amplification with adaptive moment constraint\n   - TemperatureSweep: From 0.4 to 0.1, score acceptance by Pigeonhole principle\n   - RestartSchedule: Triggered on plateau or gradient failure\n\n5. Budget and Robustness:\n   - TotalIterations: 200 if constrained, 150 otherwise\n   - Validation: Feasibility check: sum(h) \u2248 n/2 and max(h)-min(h) \u2264 1\n   - ProgressiveTimeout: Each restart \u2264 timefraction * total_budget\n   - GradientFallback: Poisson adaptive grid fallback if VOF failure \u22653 instances\n\n6. Validation and Convergence:\n   - Reevaluate all candidates using `np.correlate(h,1-h,mode='full')`\n   - Cross-check with compactness measure: L1 penalties reduced by \u226525%\n   - FinalFallback: Concat\u00e9nate best found and current trial for scoring\n   - OMPReconstruction: For broken steps, use Gaussian smoothing with \u03c3=0.02",
